            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral Vidian neurectomy--indications and results.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>235-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Indications and results of 125 Vidian neurectomies done in 64 patients have been presented. The indications were grouped as: Rhinorrhoea (37.5%), Nasal Polyposis (3.12%); Headaches and Faceaches (45.32%); and Bronchial Asthma (14-06%). Four initial Vidian neurectomies were done unilaterally and produced only partial relief in symptoms. Bilateral Vidian neurectomy relieved completely all the rhinorrhoea cases, all the nasal polyposis cases, 79-3% of headache and faceache cases and 55-5% of bronchial asthma cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
